Agents panel: limit meters read as room left, with a pace line, and a
model-scoped window (Fable Weekly) gets its own row.

Local change for this machine, not an upstream fix. The owner wants every
provider's limit bars to drain the same way and to show pace the way T3 Code's
usage view does: the bar is the share left, a hairline marks the share of the
window's time left (even pace), and the tooltip says ahead of, on or under pace
within 5 points. For Claude and Codex, an exhausted weekly allowance blocks
the session row and suppresses its pace marker. Failed refreshes visibly
mark retained readings as stale. The usage records keep the share used. Strings use I18n.t
fallbacks, so no translation file is touched.

Paths are relative to /usr (Omarchy's shell/ installs as /usr/share/omarchy/shell).

